  "$comment": "Router-bench fixture: hand-authored routing cases for the cheap-role classification the Smart Router stage 1-2 makes (SPECS §3.3). Every case asserts only fields the router's own vocabulary decides — intent (required), and where the answer is unambiguous the subject-area category. Follow-up cases carry a bounded prior-turn window and assert the resolved classification, not sub-query text (the deterministic decomposition layer owns that). Ground truths are hand-authored from the same vocabulary the domain pack narrows replies with (INTENTS, SUBJECT_AREAS); the fixture stays v0-draft until the owner signs the content off. All question and turn text is original fixture prose — no corpus excerpt.",
